WEBVTT

00:00.567 --> 00:01.867
Welcome to this short video on

00:01.967 --> 00:04.667
how to perform intermittent catheterization.

00:04.667 --> 00:06.967
Education and training can help you feel more

00:06.967 --> 00:11.267
confident and enable you to achieve successful catheterization.

00:11.267 --> 00:13.567
You can use this stepbystep video on how

00:13.567 --> 00:16.167
to catheterize with LoFric Origo to support and

00:16.167 --> 00:18.667
follow on from any training given.

00:18.667 --> 00:20.467
Always make sure you follow the advice and

00:20.567 --> 00:22.867
instructions given by your clinician, which is based

00:22.867 --> 00:25.867
on your individual medical and lifestyle needs.

00:25.867 --> 00:28.467
It's quite usual to feel a little anxious and

00:28.467 --> 00:31.267
worried about starting something new for the first time.

00:31.267 --> 00:32.867
Remember that most men who perform

00:32.967 --> 00:36.167
intermittent catheterization find the procedure lifechanging

00:36.167 --> 00:37.367
and easy to perform.

00:37.567 --> 00:39.967
With practice and support, you will soon become

00:39.967 --> 00:43.267
more confident, and intermittent catheterization will become a

00:43.267 --> 00:46.467
natural part of your daily routine.

00:46.467 --> 00:48.267
Start and end the procedure by washing

00:48.267 --> 00:50.067
your hands thoroughly with soap and water.

00:50.167 --> 00:54.067
Hand sanitizer or wet wipes can also be used.

00:54.067 --> 00:56.067
Remember to clean the tip of your penis.

00:56.167 --> 00:57.867
Your clinician can advise you on

00:57.867 --> 01:00.067
a recommended routine for this.

01:00.067 --> 01:02.767
Inside the packaging, there's a sachet with salt solution

01:02.867 --> 01:04.967
you need to squeeze or press to release the

01:04.967 --> 01:11.167
salt solution. The catheter is ready to use.

01:11.167 --> 01:13.267
Pull the tab down to open.

01:13.267 --> 01:14.867
After the package is opened, the

01:14.967 --> 01:17.167
catheter can be taken out.

01:17.167 --> 01:20.167
The packaging has an adhesive tab on the reverse side, which

01:20.167 --> 01:25.467
can be used to attach it to a dry, clean surface.

01:25.467 --> 01:29.167
Position yourself by a toilet and pass any urine, if you're able.

01:29.167 --> 01:31.267
Remove the catheter from the package.

01:31.267 --> 01:33.367
You can pull and adjust the insertion grip to

01:33.367 --> 01:37.167
control insertion without having to touch the catheter tube.

01:37.167 --> 01:39.567
Use your dominant hand to hold the catheter and

01:39.567 --> 01:42.667
use your nondominant hand to hold your penis.

01:42.667 --> 01:44.567
Lift it towards your stomach to straighten

01:44.667 --> 01:47.067
out the urethra and locate the opening.

01:47.067 --> 01:49.267
Slowly and gently insert the

01:49.267 --> 01:51.267
catheter into your urethra.

01:51.267 --> 01:53.067
You may feel some slight resistance as

01:53.167 --> 01:55.467
the catheter reaches your prostate area or

01:55.467 --> 01:59.467
at the sphincter and entrance to your bladder.

01:59.467 --> 02:01.767
If you feel a little tense, find a

02:01.767 --> 02:04.867
good position, cough a little and relax.

02:04.867 --> 02:07.367
Continue gently.

02:07.367 --> 02:10.167
Once urine starts to flow, angle the penis down

02:10.167 --> 02:12.967
and insert the catheter a further 2 to 3 centimeters,

02:12.967 --> 02:15.667
to ensure both eyelids are inside the bladder.

02:15.667 --> 02:18.367
When the urine stops flowing and slows to a drip,

02:18.367 --> 02:21.967
gently and slowly withdraw the catheter a little bit.

02:21.967 --> 02:24.267
If urine starts to flow again, wait until

02:24.267 --> 02:27.167
it is stopped to ensure complete bladder emptying.

02:27.167 --> 02:30.467
Then remove the catheter completely.

02:30.467 --> 02:32.867
The unique LoFric surface coating will ensure

02:32.967 --> 02:39.767
the catheter is still smoothly lubricated.

02:39.767 --> 02:41.767
After you put the catheter back in the

02:41.867 --> 02:47.167
package and dispose appropriately, local regulations may vary.

02:47.167 --> 02:48.967
Your clinician will advise you on

02:48.967 --> 02:51.367
how often to perform intermittent catheterization

02:51.367 --> 02:53.567
based on your individual conditions.

02:53.667 --> 02:55.967
This will, of course, depend on factors such as how

02:55.967 --> 02:58.367
your bladder works, how often you have to catheterize,

02:58.367 --> 03:00.967
how much you drink each day, and other factors.

03:00.967 --> 03:03.967
Remember, LoFric Origo is a urinary catheter

03:03.967 --> 03:06.567
designed to be used only once.

03:06.567 --> 03:09.167
Did you know LoFric Origo can easily

03:09.167 --> 03:11.067
be folded and put in your pocket so

03:11.167 --> 03:13.067
you can take it everywhere you go.

03:13.067 --> 03:14.567
LoFric Origo is ready for you,

03:14.667 --> 03:17.067
whatever your lifestyle needs.

03:17.067 --> 03:19.667
User friendly and safe in a smart package.
